  - BNGL
  - PyBNF
abstract: >-
  FluBNF forecasts weekly influenza hospital admissions for the 52 US
  jurisdictions of the CDC FluSight challenge. Its shipped forecast is an
  unfitted, equal-weight, quantile-averaged ensemble of two members: a
  sequential particle filter over an SIHRS compartmental model written in
  BNGL, fitted with a fork of PyBNF on the bngsim engine, and a calendar
  analogue. In a vintage-true retrospective of the 2023-24, 2024-25, and
  2025-26 seasons at full grid (15,460 scored cells), the ensemble scored a
  pooled weighted interval score of 0.704 relative to the CDC
  FluSight-baseline (0.848, 0.651, and 0.691 by season), beating the baseline
  in every season, and the record was replicated on independent hardware.
  Placed among the archived submissions of real FluSight teams, the same
  forecasts rank 14th of 34 (2023-24), 4th of 40 (2024-25, ahead of the
  official FluSight-ensemble), and 19th of 47 (2025-26). All scores are
  self-computed from the hub's archived vintage data and baseline files; the
  placements are retrospective replays, not real-time submissions.
